Aim
To simulate a multi server single queueing system using GPSS and analyze the performance of multiple servers sharing a single queue.

Theory
A Multi Server Single Queueing System consists of multiple servers connected to one common queue. 
Customers arrive randomly and wait in a single queue. Whenever any server becomes free, the next customer from the queue is served.
This system is widely used in supermarkets, airports, hospitals, banks, and call centers where multiple service counters are available.
In this experiment, multiple customers are generated using the GENERATE block. 
Customers first enter the queue using the QUEUE block. The SEIZE block assigns an available server to the customer. Once the service starts, the customer leaves the queue using the DEPART block.
The ADVANCE block represents the service time. After the service is completed, the RELEASE block frees the server. The TERMINATE block removes the customer from the system.

Advantages of multi-server systems:

Reduces waiting time
Improves service efficiency
Increases customer satisfaction
Handles more customers simultaneously

Applications:

Airport check-in systems
Billing counters
Hospital registration desks
Banking systems
Customer support systems

Conclusion
Thus, the simulation of a multi server single queueing system was successfully implemented. 
The experiment showed how multiple servers can reduce queue length and waiting time. The simulation report provided information about queue statistics and server utilization.
